      "local_deviation": "Cluster and ACP runner-pool administration remain visible as a native route contract in Local mode but require Cloud authority; registration tokens are never synthesized or cached by the renderer.",
      "judgment_rationale": "Cluster list and detail pages are direct sources for the canonical cluster control plane. Reads require tenant membership while create, update, delete, ACP pool mutation, and registration-token actions require tenant administration; no cluster:read permission exists. Desktop has no audited native implementation, and a single-machine Local runtime cannot honestly claim cluster authority."
